  "title": "fix round 1 for T-1407: treat PermissionError from os.killpg like ProcessLookupError (security review T-1415; folds T-1414)",
  "spec": "Fix round for T-1407, requested by security review T-1415 (request_changes): with the wall-clock deadline loop, os.killpg(proc.pid, 0) in gate._run raises PermissionError (EPERM) on macOS when the group holds only zombies; the reviewer reproduced it in tests/test_gate_timeout.py test_daemon_gate_timeout_holds_as_infra_failure at gate.py:77. This fix round carries the whole T-1414 spec, which is superseded because it depended on T-1407 merging.\n\nWhy: on macOS, os.killpg(pgid, sig) raises PermissionError (EPERM), not ProcessLookupError, when every process left in the group is a zombie. orchestrator/gate.py _run catches only ProcessLookupError around each killpg (lines ~51, 58, 65-66, 71). On 2026-10-01 T-1408's gate went red on tests/test_gate_timeout.py test_cleanup_command_runs_on_timeout with PermissionError at gate.py:65 (the os.killpg(proc.pid, 0) probe after the SIGTERM grace). In production the same race crashes run_gate on a timeout instead of returning timed_out, which the daemon would record as a gate failure.\n\nWhat: in gate._run treat PermissionError exactly like ProcessLookupError at every os.killpg call (the group is gone or unkillable zombies; reap with proc.wait/communicate as today). Keep the return shape and the wall-clock deadline logic from T-1407. Add the test with os.killpg patched to raise PermissionError on the probe and on SIGKILL: run_bounded on a sleeping child with a tiny timeout returns timed_out True and does not raise.\n\nWork in wt/T-1407 on task/T-1407, on top of its commits. Commit first, then run the focused test in the foreground; never background a command, never the full gate.\n\nAlso run tests/test_gate_timeout.py as a whole three times in a row in the foreground before finishing.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_gate_timeout.py::test_killpg_permission_error_is_treated_as_gone passes: with os.killpg raising PermissionError for the probe and SIGKILL, run_bounded on a timed-out child returns timed_out True without raising",
    "tests/test_gate_timeout.py::test_deadline_counts_wall_clock_sleep still passes, and tests/test_gate_timeout.py passes three runs in a row",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/T-1407 exits 0"
  ],
